  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe 43rd & 52nd Light Infantry Chronicle 1893\n£40.00\n\nSorry, this item is out of stock\n\nA chronicle of events and news of the 43rd and & 52nd Light Infantry regiments from 1893, inlcuding maps, illustrations and historical articles. The 43rd & 52nd were predecessors to the Oxfordshire Light Infantry and later Oxfordshire & Buckinghamshire Light Infantry.\n\nCompiled and Edited by Captain A. F. Mockler-Ferryman\n\nPublished 1894 - Eyre and Spottiswoode, London\n\nHardback, 270pages\n\nContents:\n\nRegimental Calendar for 1894\n\nThe Army List 1893\n\nThe Colonel of the Regiment\n\nThe 43rd Light Infantry in 1893\n\nThe 52nd Light Infantry in 1893\n\nThe Depot in 1893\n\nExtracts from the London Gazette 1893\n\nLetters to the Editor\n\nSignaling 1893\n\nMusketry 1893\n\nAthletics 1893\n\nFootball 1893\n\nCricket  1893\n\nRegimental pony Races, 52nd light Infantry\n\nOccasional Notes\n\nThe 43rd LI Dinner\n\nThe 52nd LI Dinner\n\nMiscellaneous\n\n-Late Commanding Officers, the 43rd\n\n-Late Commanding Officers the 52nd\n\n-About Waterloo\n\n-A Peninsular Letter\n\n-An Incident on the retreat to Corunna\n\n-The 52nd in Canada 1824\n\n-The Musketry Training of the 52nd 1857-1879\n-Bugler Hawthorn VC\n-India and New Zealand Notes\n-Duck Shooting among the Maoris\n-Two Poems by the late Captain Robert Glover\n-Forty Years Ago\n-An Eventful Journey\n-Two Months' Big Game Shooting\n-A Holiday in Kashmir\n-Visual Signalling\n-Army Gymnastics\n-Forty-third Relics, Heirlooms, &c.\n-War Medals\n-The Old Colours of the 43rd\n\nNotice to Correspondents\n\nIllustrations\n\nMaps\n\n \n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nBugle & Sabre VI\n£5.00 Read more\nRedcoats to Riflemen: A Short History of the Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire County Regiment\n£4.50 Add to cart\nMister Brownrigg’s Boys: Magdalen College School and the Great War\n£15.00 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre VIII\n£5.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
